From 16a20613686dd38c72aedbf65f8d236dc05b1639 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:28:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: address pre-SIH security deployment and AI confidence
 blockers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Scoped remediation of the seven confirmed pre-SIH blockers from the
independent audit. No architectural refactoring; the components the audit
identified as sound are untouched.
C-1 / L-11 — web container ran a dev server exposing dev auth
  web.Dockerfile now builds with `npm ci` + `npm run build` and serves with
  `npm run start` as a non-root user. /api/auth/dev-token defaults CLOSED:
  it requires ARGUS_ENABLE_DEV_AUTH=true, refuses when APP_ENV or NODE_ENV
  is production, has no built-in credentials, compares them in constant
  time, is POST-only with Cache-Control: no-store, and mints ADMIN only
  under a separate ARGUS_DEV_AUTH_ALLOW_ADMIN opt-in. The published
  password was removed from TopNav and SessionRequired.
C-3 / C-4 — intelligence service open by default, optional storage roots
  require_auth now fails closed: anonymous access needs an explicit opt-in
  AND a local APP_ENV. Startup refuses outright in a non-local environment
  with no key. Added an unauthenticated /livez so orchestrators can probe
  liveness without the credential. ARGUS_ALLOWED_STORAGE_ROOTS is mandatory
  outside local development, closing the arbitrary local file read reachable
  through /rag-ingest and /classify-document. /evaluate-bid now resolves
  document URIs through the same guarded path as every other endpoint.
C-5 — deployment did not apply migrations, and health was green regardless
  Added a one-shot `migrate` service running `alembic upgrade head`, which
  api and worker gate on via service_completed_successfully. Forward-only:
  no create_all, downgrade, stamp, drop or reset. /health/readiness now
  probes core tables so a schema-less database reports degraded, and the
  api healthcheck uses readiness rather than liveness. /health is unchanged
  as the liveness probe.
H-8 — wrong URLs for remote and container deployment
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is a build argument (it is inlined into the
  browser bundle) instead of a baked-in localhost. api and worker address
  the intelligence service as http://intelligence:8100 over the compose
  network, including the previously unset ARGUS_INTELLIGENCE_RAG_URL. No
  real hostname is committed to source.
H-12 / H-13 / H-2 — demo path was broken end to end
  seed_demo.py rebuilt against the current models: real RequirementType
  members, real TenderRequirement columns, the required clause field, no
  create_all, and a clear failure when migrations have not been applied.
  Disposable-database guardrails are unchanged. Added text-layer PDFs of
  the demo corpus under data/demo/pdf/ (generated by
  scripts/generate_demo_pdfs.py) so it passes the strict upload validator,
  which is deliberately left strict. REVIEW_REQUIRED is now terminal on
  both sides via a single shared constant, and SSE connections have a hard
  duration cap.
H-14 — unpinned intelligence dependencies
  Added requirements.in as the source of truth and
  scripts/freeze-requirements.sh, which resolves it inside the service's own
  base image. The lock itself could not be generated here (PyPI egress is
  blocked in the authoring environment), so requirements.txt is annotated
  as not yet locked and must be regenerated once before the demo.
C-6 — low-confidence AI facts could produce a definitive PASS
  /extract-document now reports review_required and low_confidence_fields on
  the contract-mode path the backend actually uses; previously both were
  computed and then dropped. The signals flow through AIServiceResult into
  each fact's metadata and into the extraction audit event, and a run with
  low-confidence fields completes as REVIEW_REQUIRED. ComplianceEngine gains
  one new precedence step: when an outcome would rest solely on an extracted
  fact below the confidence threshold, with no corroborating registry
  verification, it returns REVIEW_REQUIRED / LOW_CONFIDENCE_EVIDENCE instead
  of a definitive result. Human-attested facts are exempt, the existing
  precedence chain is unchanged, and FactRead.confidence still defaults to
  1.0 so prior behaviour is preserved.
Verification: 78 engine tests pass dynamically (21 new, 57 pre-existing
regression), plus storage-hardening, demo-PDF and end-to-end demo pipeline
checks. Backend HTTP, intelligence HTTP and frontend build could not be run
in the authoring environment — PyPI and the npm registry are both blocked by
egress policy. See the PR description for the per-item verification status.
